    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d76e8c1b_41f20706",
        "filename": "telephony/java/android/telephony/CarrierConfigManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 2038,
      "author": {
        "id": 1148298
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-12-11T18:26:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the user get the bundle before carrier B is loaded, the API will return true since it is the bundle from carrier A (currently identified by platform), right? When carrier B config is loaded, the user will receive the broadcast saying the carrier config has been changed, and the API will also return true since it is now the carrier B config (now carrier B is identified by platform).",
      "parentUuid": "1e210fa5_d8327e62",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2034,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 2038,
        "endChar": 69
      },
      "revId": "67abd019eb0a4473d15b81da3e5049584ac284bc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9b9af752_24a6262f",
        "filename": "telephony/java/android/telephony/CarrierConfigManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 2042,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060151
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-12-09T01:17:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How does the app know that the bundle is for any particular carrier?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2041,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 2042,
        "endChar": 68
      },
      "revId": "67abd019eb0a4473d15b81da3e5049584ac284bc",
